    <spell-site-header root="../../.."></spell-site-header>
    <div class="spell-doc">
      <main class="spell-doc-main">
        <!--
          TOPIC PAGE:  made by `yarn goals new`;  rules in `goals/AGENTS.md`.
          - Structured parts (items, status, history, updated) go through `yarn goals ...`;  hand-edit prose only.
          - Section ids are fixed:  other topics link to them.
        -->
        <ui-breadcrumb class="spell-crumbs" size="small" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <ui-breadcrumb-section href="../../index.html" target="_self">Goals</ui-breadcrumb-section>
          <ui-breadcrumb-section href="../index.html" target="_self">spell</ui-breadcrumb-section>
          <ui-breadcrumb-section active>14 · programmers</ui-breadcrumb-section>
        </ui-breadcrumb>
        <header class="goals-hero">
          <span class="goals-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true"><ui-icon name="laptop code"></ui-icon></span>
          <p class="goals-eyebrow"><span class="goals-num">14</span> Topic · programmers</p>
          <h1>Programmers</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Spell for developers: why they'd care, how they'll extend and embed it, and outputs beyond JavaScript, like
            Python.
          </p>
          <ui-list class="spell-meta">
            <ui-item icon="flag"
              >Status: <ui-label class="goals-status" size="mini" color="grey">draft</ui-label> · first pass, not yet
              talked through</ui-item
            >
            <ui-item icon="calendar">Updated: <time class="goals-updated">2026-10-01</time></ui-item>
            <ui-item icon="robot"
              >Notes for agents:
              <a href="programmers.md" target="src-goals-programmers-programmers-md">programmers.md</a></ui-item
            >
          </ui-list>
        </header>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="summary"><ui-icon name="eye"></ui-icon> 1. Summary</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Programmers matter three ways:</strong> they extend spell (rules and libraries), embed it (as
              their app's scripting language), and judge it (credibility, contributions).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Today:</strong> JavaScript output only; rules in TypeScript; the cli, language server and VS Code
              extension work from a checkout.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Python</strong> is an aspiration (the readme; the 2017 talk named Java and Swift). A second target
              would plug in where the syntax tree becomes JavaScript.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="today"><ui-icon name="calendar"></ui-icon> 2. Today</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Output:</strong> <code>&lt;Project&gt;.compiled.js</code>, a readable ES module on the
              <code>spellCore</code> runtime.
            </li>
            <li><strong>"Show Compiled JavaScript":</strong> in VS Code, the spell beside its JavaScript.</li>
            <li>
              <strong>The parser is general:</strong>
              <a href="../../../packages/parser/" target="src-packages-parser"><code>packages/parser</code></a> knows no
              language; rulex rules read like regular expressions for words.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>VS Code extension:</strong> needs the checkout (it runs the repo's <code>tsx</code> on the
              language server); not on the Marketplace.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="goals"><ui-icon name="bullseye"></ui-icon> 3. Goals</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <section class="s3">
            <ui-sticky class="spell-h3"
              ><h3 id="now"><ui-icon name="seedling"></ui-icon> Now → December 2026</h3></ui-sticky
            >
            <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="goal" data-horizon="now">
              <li data-status="open" id="g1">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g1">G1</a> <span class="plan-title">A page for programmers</span>
                <span class="goals-note">why spell, how it works, how to extend it</span>
              </li>
              <li data-status="open" id="g2">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g2">G2</a> <span class="plan-title">VS Code extension, installable</span>
                <span class="goals-note">from the Marketplace or Open VSX, no checkout</span>
              </li>
              <li data-status="open" id="g3">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g3">G3</a> <span class="plan-title">Output a programmer would accept</span>
                <span class="goals-note">readable JavaScript; TypeScript later (precedence plan phase 7)</span>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </section>
          <section class="s3">
            <ui-sticky class="spell-h3"
              ><h3 id="next"><ui-icon name="tree"></ui-icon> 2027</h3></ui-sticky
            >
            <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="goal" data-horizon="next">
              <li data-status="open" id="g4">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g4">G4</a> <span class="plan-title">Python, a prototype</span>
                <span class="goals-note">FizzBuzz and Todos' logic as Python</span>
              </li>
              <li data-status="open" id="g5">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g5">G5</a> <span class="plan-title">Embed spell</span>
                <span class="goals-note">an API to compile spell against your own things</span>
              </li>
              <li data-status="open" id="g6">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g6">G6</a> <span class="plan-title">Rules in spell?</span>
                <span class="goals-note">define new syntax without TypeScript</span>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </section>
          <section class="s3">
            <ui-sticky class="spell-h3"
              ><h3 id="someday"><ui-icon name="mountain sun"></ui-icon> Someday</h3></ui-sticky
            >
            <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="goal" data-horizon="someday">
              <li data-status="open" id="g7">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g7">G7</a> <span class="plan-title">More targets</span>
                <span class="goals-note">Swift, Kotlin</span>
              </li>
              <li data-status="open" id="g8">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g8">G8</a> <span class="plan-title">Spell in notebooks</span>
                <span class="goals-note">spell cells in Jupyter</span>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </section>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="ideas"><ui-icon name="lightbulb"></ui-icon> 4. Ideas</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="idea">
            <li data-status="open" id="i1">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#i1">I1</a> <span class="plan-title">Spell as a scripting language</span>
              <span class="goals-note"
                >like AppleScript or Lua for your app: you provide the things, people script them in English</span
              >
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="i2">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#i2">I2</a> <span class="plan-title">English beside the code</span>
              <span class="goals-note">show both; programmers trust what they can see</span>
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="i3">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#i3">I3</a> <span class="plan-title">Python from the same tree</span>
              <span class="goals-note"
                >a <code>toPython()</code> beside each node's <code>toJS()</code>; a Python
                <code>spellCore</code> twin</span
              >
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="i4">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#i4">I4</a> <span class="plan-title">The parser as its own product</span>
              <span class="goals-note">rulex lets anyone build an English-like language for their domain</span>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="questions"><ui-icon name="circle question"></ui-icon> 5. Questions</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="question">
            <li data-status="open" id="q1">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#q1">Q1</a> <span class="plan-title">Why Python?</span>
              <span class="goals-note">data people? teaching? servers?</span
              ><ui-accordion class="spell-aside" styled
                ><ui-title>details</ui-title
                ><ui-content
                  ><p>
                    The runtime (<code>spellCore</code>) would need a Python twin: that's the real cost, more than the
                    compiler.
                  </p>
                </ui-content></ui-accordion
              >
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="q2">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#q2">Q2</a> <span class="plan-title">Which programmers first?</span>
              <span class="goals-note">those who embed, extend, or contribute?</span>
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="q3">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#q3">Q3</a> <span class="plan-title">Is the parser a product?</span>
              <span class="goals-note"><code>@spell-app/parser</code> and rulex, on their own</span>
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="q4">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#q4">Q4</a>
              <span class="plan-title">TypeScript output: for the editor, or for people?</span>
              <span class="goals-note">the plan uses it only for editor checks</span>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="risks"><ui-icon name="triangle exclamation"></ui-icon> 6. Risks</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="risk">
            <li data-status="open" id="r1">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#r1">R1</a> <span class="plan-title">"English-like" has a reputation</span>
              <span class="goals-note">AppleScript's: position spell as readable, not "easy"</span>
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="r2">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#r2">R2</a> <span class="plan-title">A second target doubles the runtime</span>
              <span class="goals-note">every feature, twice</span>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="decisions"><ui-icon name="gavel"></ui-icon> 7. Decisions</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="decision"></ol>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="work"><ui-icon name="list check"></ui-icon> 8. Work</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="work">
            <li data-status="open" id="w1">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#w1">W1</a> <span class="plan-title">Package the VS Code extension</span>
              <span class="goals-note">bundle the language server; no <code>tsx</code>, no repo path</span>
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="w2">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#w2">W2</a> <span class="plan-title">Python spike: FizzBuzz</span>
              <span class="goals-note">a few node types to Python, to size the work</span>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="history"><ui-icon name="clock rotate left"></ui-icon> 9. History</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ui-feed class="spell-history goals-history" size="small"
            ><ui-event icon="pen to square"
              ><ui-content
                ><ui-summary
                  >Page made: a first pass from the code, the 2017 talk and old notes
                  <ui-date>2026-10-01</ui-date></ui-summary
                ></ui-content
              ></ui-event
            ></ui-feed
          >
